# The free demo's configuration: who ships it, and where they live.
#
# `check:env` requires the keys-only contract from every app. This was empty and honestly so: every
# page renders from fixtures in its own file, so there is no API to point at, no database, no auth and
# nothing secret. Its own URL is not configuration either, since it is built into the marketing site's
# `public/` and served at `/preview/free-react`, a path that is correct in every environment.
#
# The footer is the exception. A buyer shipping this template is not Viliha, and saying so should be
# two keys rather than a component edit, which is the difference between a template and a fork. The
# name is rendered verbatim: casing is part of how a company writes its own name.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_NAME=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=
